{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01OO", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-properties-rings}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:14707c922edbd3fd70b6a276dd6c6939522825b6295ae73f1d56e48aa2f7abcd", "source_text": "Types of schemes defined by properties of rings", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7235959975a66d8c24739d124ddba99ba46c6236acd408554fdcbabb47bb9cdd", "unit_id": "tag:01OO:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01OO", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cc2a9fa570e406ab2fcce2ab8accf6732156282e7e80c5bccdf66d860b265ddd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we study what properties of rings\nallow one to define local properties of schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:89d4797b59cc601a4716762346a033fee21254da1a453f1e4d3b2dbb4a081198", "unit_id": "tag:01OO:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01OO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$P$", "MATH_0002": "$P$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$f \\in R$", "MATH_0005": "$P(R) \\Rightarrow P(R_f)$", "MATH_0006": "$R$", "MATH_0007": "$f_i \\in R$", "MATH_0008": "$(f_1, \\ldots, f_n) = R$", "MATH_0009": "$\\forall i, P(R_{f_i}) \\Rightarrow P(R)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-property-local}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d8e25e83279730e021bae22ade4b033066ca48ddb22bae3874b4bab9d2ebe2e5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:118a9984c1a17d117676c608f2ac8402de268ac0ceceb9c6ab7de7208c2152fc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a property of rings.\nWe say that <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>local<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the following hold:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> For any ring <MATH_0003>, and any <MATH_0004> we have\n<MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0003> For any ring <MATH_0006>, and <MATH_0007> such that\n<MATH_0008> then\n<MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:45b76b3d0f74819937fc2e015e8a106db3bb72524ecf884538bb5ed9f83c9998", "unit_id": "tag:01OP:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01OO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$P$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$P$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0010": "$P$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-locally-P}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d4f9df05f28e77ed4a5f0c6a2db3e9ae6eb2448847853a5ce44fb804ee65e423", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f01a6acf7c8b93f82488ee547a6d541be049a6e52a8c4e5307b088a97131ead1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a property of rings. Let <MATH_0002> be a scheme.\nWe say <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>locally <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for any <MATH_0005>\nthere exists an affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007>\nin <MATH_0008> such that <MATH_0009> has property <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:60c72780f8c357f418119fe433cdffc9f4bb0fe5ebf5de0e02f2c9d161c8aaf6", "unit_id": "tag:01OQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01OO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$P$", "MATH_0002": "$P$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:23a315330a8a4ed17f5950863e8c38255614b61f27087dd3d4f16204a811340f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a67fc17f9d71209ec30ec1669f22c0af5cb58aa6be2fa08b49f155a690d9e02c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is only a good notion if the property is local.\nEven if <MATH_0001> is a local property we will not\nautomatically use this definition to say that a scheme is\n``locally <MATH_0002>'' unless we also explicitly state the definition\nelsewhere.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:90aa2e9b242e043fa337c1ca96fc8e808cc66c201cbe17eb0f898ff4d69cf0b6", "unit_id": "tag:01OO:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$P$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$P$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0006": "$P(\\mathcal{O}_X(U))$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0009": "$P$", "MATH_0010": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0011": "$X_j$", "MATH_0012": "$P$", "MATH_0013": "$X$", "MATH_0014": "$P$", "MATH_0015": "$P$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-P}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f68f34808f8c5d4fbbb69e7dbcbb73e4fd2627fc241da6fd43bc29647fa848f0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:780b73b8200e2335b00da15cce7c6bf9516d9d20e5c92c946ed98c9fc0ae2f93", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a local property of rings.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0003> is locally <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0005> the property\n<MATH_0006> holds.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0007> such that\neach <MATH_0008> satisfies <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0010>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0011> is locally <MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0013> is locally <MATH_0014> then every open subscheme\nis locally <MATH_0015>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ffba01d1ac7439f5a2b91c54dc5eb59463fb9fb4e96ca760509ff657d2871edf", "unit_id": "tag:01OR:statement"}
